On May 13, 7:47 pm, Henry J Cobb <h...@io.com> wrote:

> The protection of the Mitre is already class restricted so that's a
> second class locked artifact.

Partially locked; non-priests still get the energy boost from
invoking, and fire resistance should you actually need an external
source of that. The Knight's quest item also has double-damage
abilities that only work with that class.

Going along these lines (as I do agree with some of Derek Ray's points
against adding more conducts), it seems the remainder of the quest
artifacts could be limited in some way to make them less useful to
wish for. The Orb and Eye's level porting are probably the most useful
aspects of those artifacts; perhaps those could be class-restricted,
or alternatively, the half damage from the Orb could be limited to
Valkyries, and the magic resistance and/or spell regeneration of the
Eye limited to Wizards. The Staff of Aesculapius could restrict either
drain resistance or hungerless regeneration to Healers. The Sceptre of
Might could restrict either magic resistance or hungerless conflict to
Cavemen. Etc.

